diagnosis_text:
Affected component: dynamic routing (FRRouting/RIP) on router2, not the physical WAN. After maintenance, FRR on router2 is stopped, so router2 no longer learns any 192.168.x.x routes.

Mechanism: Hosts in the Server Room (1.0.0.0/8) and Internet Lab (128.168.0.0/16) forward off-subnet traffic to router2. Because router2 lacks routes to 192.168.x.x, it immediately generates ICMP “Destination Net Unreachable,” which we observe when pinging 192.168.3.2: “From 1.0.0.1 … Net Unreachable” (pc1) and “From 128.168.0.1 … Net Unreachable” (pc2). Intra-zone traffic remains fine, matching the report.

Localization: router2’s control plane. Evidence:
- router2 routing table has only connected networks: 1.0.0.0/8 (eth0), 128.168.
